.TH TMOE 1 "2026-03-22" "2.0.0" "TMOE Manual"
.SH NAME
tmoe \- Manage Linux containers and GUI desktop environments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmoe
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TMOE
(TMOE, More Optional Environments) is a tool for managing Linux containers
and GUI desktop environments, especially on Android/Termux.
.PP
This is the Python 3.10+ rewrite with a modern TUI interface.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "p, proot"
Manage Proot containers (no root required)
.TP
.BR "c, chroot"
Manage Chroot containers (root required)
.TP
.BR "d, docker"
Manage Docker containers
.TP
.BR "ls, list"
List installed containers
.TP
.BR "t, tool"
Open tools menu
.TP
.BR "m, manager"
Launch TUI manager (default)
.TP
.BR "zsh"
Manage Zsh configuration
.TP
.BR "aria2"
Manage aria2 downloader
.TP
.BR "theme"
Manage Zsh themes
.TP
.BR "-h, --help"
Show help message
.TP
.BR "-v, --version"
Show version information
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR "--debug"
Enable debug mode
.TP
.BR "--verbose"
Enable verbose output
.TP
.BR "--locale " \fILOCALE\fR
Set locale (e.g., zh_CN, en_US)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch TUI manager:
.B tmoe
.TP
Create a new Proot Debian container:
.B tmoe p debian
.TP
List all containers:
.B tmoe ls
.TP
Start a specific container:
.B tmoe p start debian
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tmoe-linux/config.json
User configuration file
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tmoe-linux/containers/
Container storage directory (Android/Termux)
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/tmoe-linux/
System-wide configuration directory
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMOE_LOCALE
Default locale setting
.TP
.B TMOE_DEBUG
Enable debug mode when set to 1
